//# #2745: the same local lambda with its return type left OFF.
//
// Self-probed while fixing round 15, and it is the reason that fix has two
// halves. The annotated `[U](u: U) -> U { u }` answers from the declared
// return; `[U](u: U) { u }` has no `ret` to read and still printed a 3-digit
// pointer decimal after that fix landed. The annotation is not what makes the
// answer available.
//
// A body that IS a parameter returns that parameter's value, so the call's
// classification is that argument's -- whatever the types are. That needs no
// type-parameter check, because it is not an inference about the return TYPE;
// it is the observation that the value is the argument. One syntactic shape,
// no environment consulted.
//
// This fixture also records a COST. Five earlier fixtures used a local generic
// as "the initializer this walk declines", which is what isolated the route
// each was written for. That value is no longer opaque, so those five now
// refuse for two reasons instead of one -- see their headers. The supply of
// unclassifiable expressions shrinks every round, and with it the ability to
// pin a route in isolation; that is a cost of enumeration, recorded in #2773.

struct Qt {
  w: Int
}

fn outer[T](x: T) -> String {
  let inner = [T](a: T) -> String {
    let opq = [U](u: U) {
      u
    }
    "\{opq(a)}"
  }
  inner(Qt::{ w: 5 })
}

export fn _start() -> Int {
  String::length(outer(7))
}
